---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE_NAME } from '../config';
---

<BaseLayout
  searchType="Pages"
  title={`Sources and licensing | ${SITE_NAME}`}
  description="Every data source behind Samvidhan and its license: the official PDF, amendment facts, bill tracking, and code."
>
  <div class="container page">
    <p class="kicker">Sources</p>
    <h1>Sources and licensing</h1>

    <dl class="sources">
      <dt>Constitution text</dt>
      <dd>
        The official Legislative Department PDF
        (<a href="https://www.legislative.gov.in/constitution-of-india">legislative.gov.in</a>), edition as on 1 May
        2026, vendored into this repository at data/source/. Statutes are public domain under Indian law (EBC v. D.B.
        Modak, 2008), so the text carries no license obligation. The text is never altered; editorial markers are
        stripped only for display.
      </dd>

      <dt>Amendment facts</dt>
      <dd>
        Years and milestones are derived from Wikipedia's List of amendments of the Constitution of India (CC BY-SA
        4.0, attributed), paraphrased. Wherever the official PDF's own citations survive (97 of 106 amendments), the
        PDF is the source of record. Summaries on landmark amendment pages are written for this site.
      </dd>

      <dt>Bill tracking</dt>
      <dd>
        Pending bills are paraphrased from
        <a href="https://sansad.in">sansad.in</a> (official) and
        <a href="https://prsindia.org/billtrack">prsindia.org/billtrack</a>, snapshotted by hand every month. Each row
        links to its source and shows its last verified date. No analysis text is copied.
      </dd>

      <dt>Plain words summaries</dt>
      <dd>
        Original editorial content by this project, licensed CC BY 4.0. They are summaries, never legal advice, and
        never a substitute for the text of the Constitution.
      </dd>

      <dt>Code</dt>
      <dd>Released under the MIT license. See LICENSE in the repository.</dd>

      <dt>Community datasets, evaluated and rejected</dt>
      <dd>
        GitHub datasets of the Constitution (captn3m0, civictech-India) were reviewed and rejected: last updated 2019
        to 2021, and two of the three carry no license. The MIT licensed Yash Handa JSON is used as a structural cross
        check only, never as published text.
      </dd>
    </dl>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page {
    padding: var(--space-12) var(--space-4) var(--space-16);
    max-width: 46rem;
  }

  .kicker {
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    font-size: var(--text-body-s);
    color: var(--color-navy);
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: var(--text-display-l);
    color: var(--color-navy);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  dt {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: var(--text-heading-s);
    color: var(--color-navy);
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
  }

  dd {
    margin: var(--space-2) 0 0;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  a {
    color: var(--color-link);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
</style>
